{
  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "The workflow already implements the applicable safe optimizations: path-scoped push/pull_request triggers (P-LIT-CHANGE-FILTER), a concurrency group with cancel-in-progress that supersedes stale runs on the same ref (P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE), and dependency caching via setup-node cache plus actions/cache for pnpm/yarn/npm stores and the UI build (P-LIT-GHA-CACHE). P-LIT-FAIL-FAST is contraindicated: the test-app and test-ae matrices each cover distinct configurations (installer x script x engine x linter x flags), so every matrix outcome is required for coverage and the workflow deliberately sets fail-fast: false; switching to true would cancel remaining jobs and reduce failure diagnostics. P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT lacks per-job successful-duration history (only workflow-level history is available) and risks false timeouts on valid slow runs, so a specific timeout cannot be justified. P-LIT-SKIP-WORKFLOW has negligible reported impact (<0.1%) and requires an omission policy that is not present.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-GHA-CACHE", "P-LIT-FAIL-FAST", "P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE", "P-LIT-CHANGE-FILTER", "P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT", "P-LIT-SKIP-WORKFLOW"]
}
